From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: bcm-pdc: check ring space before mapping a message

pdc_send_data() maps both scatterlists of a message and only then checks
whether the rings have room for its descriptors. If not, it returns
-ENOSPC without unmapping them. The mailbox framework keeps the message
queued and calls pdc_send_data() again later, which maps the same
scatterlists again. The first mappings are never released, and with
CONFIG_DMA_API_DEBUG the second mapping is reported as an overlapping
mapping.

Check the ring space first. The descriptor count uses only the
scatterlist lengths, so it does not need the mapping.

Fixes: ab8d1b2d564f ("mailbox: bcm-pdc: Convert from interrupts to poll for tx done")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mailbox/bcm-pdc-mailbox.c | 29 +++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mailbox/bcm-pdc-mailbox.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/bcm-pdc-mailbox.c
@@ -1203,6 +1203,21 @@ static int pdc_send_data(struct mbox_chan *chan, void *data)
 	if (unlikely(mssg->type != BRCM_MESSAGE_SPU))
 		return -ENOTSUPP;
 
+	/*
+	 * Check if the tx and rx rings have enough space. Do this prior to
+	 * mapping the message or writing any tx or rx descriptors: the
+	 * message stays queued in the mailbox framework and is sent again
+	 * later. Need to ensure that we do not write a partial set of
+	 * descriptors, or write just rx descriptors but corresponding tx
+	 * descriptors don't fit. Note that we want this check and the entire
+	 * sequence of descriptor to happen without another thread getting in.
+	 * The channel spin lock in the mailbox framework ensures this.
+	 */
+	tx_desc_req = pdc_desc_count(mssg->spu.src);
+	rx_desc_req = pdc_desc_count(mssg->spu.dst);
+	if (unlikely(pdc_rings_full(pdcs, tx_desc_req, rx_desc_req + 1)))
+		return -ENOSPC;
+
 	src_nent = sg_nents(mssg->spu.src);
 	if (likely(src_nent)) {
 		nent = dma_map_sg(dev, mssg->spu.src, src_nent, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
@@ -1221,20 +1236,6 @@ static int pdc_send_data(struct mbox_chan *chan, void *data)
 		}
 	}
 
-	/*
-	 * Check if the tx and rx rings have enough space. Do this prior to
-	 * writing any tx or rx descriptors. Need to ensure that we do not write
-	 * a partial set of descriptors, or write just rx descriptors but
-	 * corresponding tx descriptors don't fit. Note that we want this check
-	 * and the entire sequence of descriptor to happen without another
-	 * thread getting in. The channel spin lock in the mailbox framework
-	 * ensures this.
-	 */
-	tx_desc_req = pdc_desc_count(mssg->spu.src);
-	rx_desc_req = pdc_desc_count(mssg->spu.dst);
-	if (unlikely(pdc_rings_full(pdcs, tx_desc_req, rx_desc_req + 1)))
-		return -ENOSPC;
-
 	/* Create rx descriptors to SPU catch response */
 	err = pdc_rx_list_init(pdcs, mssg->spu.dst, mssg->ctx);
 	err |= pdc_rx_list_sg_add(pdcs, mssg->spu.dst);
